<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

        <title>[[title]] - Privacy Policy</title>

        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/styles.css">
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/privacy.css">
    </head>
    <body>
        <%view navbar %>
        <div id="main-content">
            <div id="privacy-title-text">[[title]] Privacy Policy</div>
            <div id="privacy-text">
                You do not have privacy here. It is the internet after all.
                <br />
                But if you're curious, <strong>what is being collected about you?</strong><br />
                <dl>
                    <dt>In the access log:</dt>
                    <dd>Your IP address</dd>
                    <dd>User agent</dd>
                    <dd>Any paths you have visited on the website</dd>

                    <dt>In the server session storage:</dt>
                    <dd>Your user's ID</dd>

                    <dt>In the rate limiter:</dt>
                    <dd>Your IP address</dd>

                    <dt>In the database:</dt>
                    <dd>Anything you submit(when editing/creating a user/comment/video) to the website</dd>
                </dl>

                <strong>Alright, what about cookies?</strong> <br />
                <strong>SessionId</strong> - Stores the token so you don't have to type your password on every single page<br />

                That is it. <br /> <br />

                <strong>Is this website GDPR compliant?</strong> <br />
                No. This website violates all online privacy laws that I know about. If that offends you, please leave. <br />
            </div>
        </div>
        <%view footer %>
    </body>
</html>
